# Titan Orbit — WebGL is the ship client

The live game is a **browser client** (IL2CPP/WASM) talking to a dedicated server over Relay **WSS**.
A Windows player or Editor Play Mode join that works is **not** a WebGL join.

Do **not** ask for a 45-minute WebGL rebuild to “see more logs.” Validate in Editor first.
One WebGL rebuild only after the change is Editor-checked and is the actual fix.

---

## Proven WASM landmines (do not reintroduce)

| Unsafe on WebGL | Use instead |
|---|---|
| `World.Update()` | `TitanOrbitWebGlClientTick.SafeUpdate` |
| `EntityManager.AddBuffer<T>` in connect / receive / scene OnCreate | `AddComponent(ComponentTypeSet)` + `GetBuffer` |
| `NetworkStreamDriver.Connect` | `TitanOrbitWebGlClientConnect.CreateConnectionEntity` + UTP `driver.Connect` |
| `NetworkGroupCommandBufferSystem` OnCreate | Local `EntityCommandBuffer` (already in Receive WebGL path) |
| Burst `IJobEntity` over `NetworkStreamConnection` | WebGL Burst AOT stays **off** (`BurstAotSettings_WebGL.json`) |
| Editing `Packages/com.unity.netcode` | Game code only |

`#if UNITY_WEBGL` is **true in the Editor** when the WebGL build target is active. Play Mode is still a desktop player (DTLS, stock `AddBuffer`). Gate player-only paths with `UNITY_WEBGL && !UNITY_EDITOR`.

---

## Before any WebGL rebuild

1. Run **TitanOrbit → WebGL → Validate Connect Entity Recipe** (seconds, no player build).
2. Do not add per-tick `WebGlBootDebugProbe` / leaf-walk logs. They force another rebuild to read.
3. If Windows works and WebGL does not, the bug is WASM / WSS / SafeUpdate — not lobby or server sim.

```csharp
// ❌ BAD — stock Connect; WebGL returns an entity index with 0 NetworkStreamConnection
driver.Connect(em, relay.Endpoint);

// ✅ GOOD — one TypeSet including ICleanupComponentData, then SetComponentData
TitanOrbitWebGlClientConnect.CreateConnectionEntity(em, utpConnection, state);
```
